  "important_caveat_discovered_this_run": "While building ground truth, empirically verified (via direct defects4j checkout -v <id>b vs -v <id>f comparison) that defects4j's Lang .src.patch files are oriented FIXED -> BUGGY, not BUGGY -> FIXED as assumed throughout this project's prior analysis. Confirmed for bugs 1, 5, and 20 directly. This means results/edit_quality_analysis.md and the 'deletion bias' finding in results/PROGRESS_SUMMARY.md have the fix direction backwards for all three worked examples -- the real fixes were additions, not deletions. The live COLLECT-phase prompt's deletion example (in prompts.py) is therefore based on a backwards example and should be corrected or removed. This does not affect method-name ground truth (method identity is direction-independent) so the localization results above are unaffected, but the deletion-bias narrative needs a follow-up correction.",
